course: dictionary
lesson: 12368
title: Food words from other languages
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words come from other languages, and food words often do. You may spot them on a menu, in a school dinner or on a frozen food box. «We had chicken croquettes and peas for school lunch.» Croquette is one of these words.
explain: Use the context to find its meaning. The words «mashed potato», «breadcrumbs» and «fried» are clues. A croquette is a small roll or ball of mashed potato, meat, fish or vegetables, covered in breadcrumbs and fried.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Dad made potato croquettes for tea, and they were crispy on the outside.» If you put in a small ball of mashed food, covered in crumbs and fried, the sentence still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Croquette» is a noun: one croquette, two croquettes.
fact: «Croquette» comes from French, and it is often seen on menus and frozen food boxes.
fact: In Spain they are called «croquetas», and they are a popular tapa, a small dish eaten with drinks.
fact: Croquettes can be made from potato, meat, fish or vegetables, and they are covered in breadcrumbs and fried.
exercise: «Ella ate three fish croquettes with her chips.» What is a croquette? | *A small roll or ball of food, covered in breadcrumbs and fried | A long thin biscuit | A type of cake with icing | A small bowl of soup
exercise: «The croquettes were golden because they were fried.» Find and copy one word that means cooked in hot fat. | *fried | croquettes | were | golden
exercise: In Spain, what are croquettes called? | Galletas | *Croquetas | Churros | Tortillas
test: Which is the plural of croquette? | croquetti | croquetters | croquette | *croquettes
test: Ben says croquettes are sweet puddings made with cream. What is wrong? | They are always made of chocolate | *They are small rolls or balls of food, covered in breadcrumbs and fried | They are cakes baked with fruit | They are drinks
exam: What covers a croquette? | *Breadcrumbs | Chocolate | Sugar | Custard
